#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""grok-verify — the gate to run after every `grok` CLI update, and the long-run soak (spec-095 P7).

    tools/grok-verify check [--login PATH] [--grok-bin PATH] [--with-cockpit] [--dry-run] ...
    tools/grok-verify soak  [--login PATH] [--duration 24h] [--interval 20m] [--cycles N] [--dry-run] ...

`check` is the CLI-bump gate. It prints `grok --version` and whether that build is on
`grok_engine.KNOWN_GOOD_VERSIONS`, then runs, against a SCRATCH GROK_HOME seeded with a copy of a
login you point it at (`--login`, env GROK_VERIFY_LOGIN, default ~/.grok):

  live      pytest -m grok_live     compat isolation, sandbox denial, the marker-file checks (a repo's
                                    own MCP server / hook / skill must start nothing), one real turn
  canary    pytest -m grok_canary   egress canary: a repo with a multi-MB blob in its git history, one
                                    "reply OK" turn, no connection may send more than 1 MiB
  cockpit   pytest -m grok_live_cockpit   (only with --with-cockpit) the whole wired cockpit driven
                                    over HTTP with the real binary
  fixtures  re-record the wire fixtures into a TEMP dir (tools/grok_record_fixtures.py) and diff the
            event TYPE / field-shape skeletons against tests/fixtures/grok/ — ids and text are
            ignored; added and removed methods and fields are listed

Only when EVERY step passed (and none was skipped by a flag) and the build is not already listed does
it print the exact one-line edit for KNOWN_GOOD_VERSIONS. It never edits a file itself.

`soak` is the long run: N cycles over a duration (default 24 h, one cycle every 20 min). Each cycle is
one tiny real turn through `grok_engine.run_grok_engine` in a scratch project under the production
sandbox profile, then asserts: no `grok agent` process of that GROK_HOME left over, the sandbox
litter count and the GROK_HOME size growth stay bounded; every K cycles it runs the egress canary.
One JSON line per cycle goes to the log file, a summary is written at the end, SIGTERM/SIGINT stop it
cleanly (the engine kills its process group, the scratch tree and the login copy are removed).
Model turns cost subscription quota: about one per cycle + one sandbox probe + one canary per K cycles.
`--cycles 2 --interval 5` is the smoke run.

`--dry-run` prints what would happen and spends nothing (it still runs `grok --version`).

Exit status: 0 = everything passed; 1 = a check failed, or the run was incomplete (a step skipped by
a flag is NOT a pass); 128+N = stopped by signal N. Output never contains the login's values.

Everything is a flag or an environment variable (nothing machine specific is in this file):
GROK_BIN, GROK_VERIFY_LOGIN, GROK_VERIFY_LOG, GROK_VERIFY_SCRATCH (parent of the scratch tree,
default $TMPDIR), GROK_VERIFY_PYTEST (test runner command, default `<python> -m pytest`),
GROK_VERIFY_RECORDER (fixture recorder command, default tools/grok_record_fixtures.py).
"""
